{
  "version": "2026-08-v1",
  "assembled_on": "2026-08-04",
  "domain": "funding",
  "amount_tolerance": 0.08,
  "window_days": 45,
  "method": [
    "The largest DISCLOSED funding rounds per quarter, one entry per round,",
    "each carrying the primary document: the company's own announcement page",
    "or its own press release. Assembled 2026-08-04 by public web research",
    "only. No commercial funding database was consulted and none may be: a",
    "landmark whose provenance is somebody else's product is a licence",
    "problem and a circular measurement at the same time.",
    "",
    "Every figure here was read off the primary document, not off a headline",
    "about it. Where the primary host refuses automated requests (openai.com",
    "and x.ai both answer 403 to every non-interactive client) the URL is",
    "still the publisher's own permalink, because that is the document; the",
    "figure was confirmed from the announcement's own text as reproduced in",
    "the search index and cross-read against two independent outlets.",
    "",
    "THIS SET IS NOT A RECALL MEASUREMENT AND MUST NEVER BE USED AS ONE.",
    "analysis/recall/ answers 'how much of the world do we hold', against a",
    "sealed set with a required geographic shape. This answers a different and",
    "much narrower question: 'are the events nobody could defend missing",
    "actually here?'. It is deliberately top-of-distribution and deliberately",
    "US and Europe heavy, because that is where the largest disclosed rounds",
    "were. Quoting a percentage from this file as coverage would be flattery.",
    "",
    "EXTENSIBLE BY HAND, ON PURPOSE. A new quarter is a human sitting down",
    "with public sources and appending entries. Nothing generates this file,",
    "and in particular nothing generates it from our own database, which is",
    "the one method that would guarantee a perfect score and measure nothing."
  ],
  "sibling_note": [
    "The layoff tracker (dk-forge/ai-layoff-tracker) needs the same guard over",
    "its own landmarks: the largest layoff EVENTS per quarter, each with",
    "company, date, headcount and the primary document (the 8-K, the WARN",
    "notice, or the employer's own statement). It is out of scope for this",
    "repository and is recorded here so the idea does not die with this",
    "session. The two trackers share no code and no database, so it is a port",
    "of the shape, not an import of the module."
  ],
  "verdict_vocabulary": {
    "HELD": "a current row matches this employer, this window and this amount",
    "WRONG_AMOUNT": "a row for this event exists but its amount is absent or off",
    "MISSING": "nothing in the corpus is this event",
    "UNKNOWN": "the lens could not be read at all, which is never a pass"
  },
